      "description": "Watch Boca Juniors vs Estudiantes L.P. highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 6, 2026. On a high-stakes night in the Liga Profesional Argentina , two traditional giants faced off in a match defined by tactical intensity and a search for an opening. The clash on August 6, 2026 , promised drama from the start as both sides looked to gain a crucial advantage in the standings. The Breakthrough Before the Break The opening half was a tightly contested affair, with midfield battles dominating the narrative and clear chances remaining at a premium. Just as the referee was preparing to blow for halftime, the deadlock was finally broken in the first minute of stoppage time. Lautaro Blanco delivered a pinpoint assist into the danger zone, allowing Santiago Ascacibar to find the back of the net. The goal gave Estudiantes L.P. a vital lead going into the interval, changing the complexion of the match entirely. Tactical Adjustments and Physical Play As the second half got underway, the intensity did not waver. Boca Juniors looked to respond, but their rhythm was often disrupted by a series of fouls and tactical cautions. Ezequiel Piovi received a yellow card in the 56th minute, signaling a more aggressive approach from both sides. Substitutions followed shortly after, with Brian Aguirre and Edwuin Cetre introduced to provide fresh energy on the flanks, while Sebastian Villa replaced Miguel Merentiel in an attempt to sharpen the attack. Tension Until the Final Whistle The closing stages were characterized by a flurry of disciplinary actions and strategic changes. Leonel Flores and Gabriel Neves were both booked as the game became increasingly fragmented. In a final roll of the dice, Lucas Alario was brought on for Piovi in the 86th minute to bolster the offensive line. Despite the late pressure and a 90th-minute yellow card for Gaston Benedetti , the defensive unit held firm. The final whistle at 90+4 minutes brought an end to a gripping contest where one decisive moment made all the difference."
